  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New catalog case `examples/catalog/multiaxis/wrapped`. The part is a 20 mm x 20 mm bar along X with one round-bottom ring groove at X0.\n- The model generator `model/gen_wrapped_obj.py` writes `wrapped.obj`. It checks that the mesh is closed and that each facet faces out.\n- `build.camscript` uses the built-in `Tormach 770MX + microARC 4` machine. It adds the setup `Wrap` with the `Tormach PathPilot` post, and a cylinder stock along X.\n- Three operations use the catalog ball mill `BN-0600`:\n  - `Wrap rough`: Rotary Offset.\n  - `Wrap finish`: Rotary Parallel. It also finishes the two end faces down to the A centreline.\n  - `Groove rings`: Rotary Contour, from X-5 to X5.\n- Each posted operation turns A. The program has no B word. Wrapped moves use `G93`, then `G94`.\n- `cargo xtask catalog` added the case link under Rotary Contour, Rotary Parallel and Rotary Offset in `site/content/guide/multi-axis/operations-multiaxis.md`.\n- The held pin from commit `cab66a8e2` moved into the `example_catalog` directory suite: `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/case_multiaxis_wrapped.rs`. No new top-level test binary remains.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2869-wrapped-case.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe catalog had no case for the three rotary kinds. The earlier attempt stopped on #3000, which is now closed.\n\n## Refusals found (filed and linked on #2392)\n\n- #2772 (already open): the rotary kinds refuse a groove that wanders along X (a barrel cam). The case uses a ring groove.\n- #4422 (new, P3): without a setup, the post refuses a B word for this A-only program. The case adds a setup as the workaround.\n- No MCP parameter was missing.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `catalog_multiaxis_wrapped::keeps_three_rotary_operations_and_posts_a_axis_moves`. It checks the three saved kinds, an `Ok` status for each, the embedded model, and A motion in each posted section.\n- Red before the case: with the case folder removed, the pin fails with `the wrapped catalog project must load: Io(... NotFound ...)`.\n- Mutation: with the A words removed from the `Groove rings` section of `wrapped.nc`, the pin fails with `each rotary operation must move the A axis`. With the file restored, it passes.\n- `catalog_multiaxis_wrapped::regenerates` and `::rebuilds` are in the heavy lane. Each takes about 30 s alone in debug. The `2d/slots` case set this precedent.\n- Commands on the final head `feec48b38` (after a merge of upstream/main `392980120`):\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 10 steps, 0 failed.\n  - `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 2 steps (heavy build, `app heavy: example_catalog`), 0 failed. The wrapped case took 10 s in that lane.\n  - `cargo xtask catalog --check`: all 17 cases checked.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n  - `cargo check --tests -p camcraft-app`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed. This ran before the merge of upstream/main. The merge changed no file of this PR except one `include!` line.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- None of the existing programs changed. `cargo xtask catalog --check` reproduces each committed `.nc` and `refusal.txt`.\n- New: `examples/catalog/multiaxis/wrapped/wrapped.nc` and `wrapped.camproj` (about 3.7 MB).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No physical machine ran the program.\n- No screenshots: the PR has no UI change.\n- The full `example_catalog` debug suite ran in the quick gate. The full heavy lanes of other crates did not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #4410 (3D rest case) adds its own `include!` line to `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`, near this one. It touches the same file, different line. Whichever merges second refreshes; the fix keeps both lines.\n- #4408 (five-axis case) changes the example blocks of other kinds (Swarf, Contour, Flow) in `site/content/guide/multi-axis/operations-multiaxis.md`. It touches the same file, different blocks. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Example catalog: new case multiaxis/wrapped, a grooved bar cut with Rotary Offset, Rotary Parallel and Rotary Contour on the A axis.\n\nFixes #2869\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
